ter must include: writer's credentials, how they know of Vedh's work (independent letters via publications/conferences), specific contributions, and industry-wide significance"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 6,\n      "title": "Phase 6 — Petition Assembly & Filing",\n      "timeline": "Months 11-14",\n      "urgency": "Critical for Filing",\n      "steps": [\n        "Engage specialized EB-1A counsel (e.g., Wegreened, Chen Immigration, North America Immigration Law Group) for petition drafting and Kazarian merits analysis",\n        "Assemble final exhibit binder: criteria-by-criteria evidence with tabbed indexing, expert letters, awards, publications, citations, salary documentation",\n        "Draft petition narrative tying together AI/Conversational Apps + Cloud Migration + Enterprise Architecture as a coherent area of extraordinary ability with sustained national/international acclaim",\n        "File I-140 with Premium Processing ($2,805) for 15-business-day adjudication; have RFE response evidence pre-staged"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  "profileRarity": {\n    "stats": [\n      {"value": "22+", "label": "Years in Enterprise Architecture", "sublabel": "Top 5% of tech leaders by tenure"},\n      {"value": "200+", "label": "Direct Reports as CTO", "sublabel": "Distinguished organizational leadership"},\n      {"value": "8+", "label": "Fortune 500 / Government Clients", "sublabel": "Molina, Cardinal Health, Voya, Nationwide, CBA, Wells Fargo, States of OH/MI"},\n      {"value": "1", "label": "Forbes Technology Council Membership", "sublabel": "Vetted invitation-based association"}\n    ],\n    "competitiveAdvantage": "Vedh's profile is distinctive in combining deep cross-industry impact (banking, healthcare, insurance, government) with formal CTO leadership, CMMI Level 3 establishment credit, and Forbes Technology Council membership. The breadth of named distinguished organizations (Commonwealth Bank, Nationwide, Voya, Wells Fargo, multiple state governments) provides unusually strong Criterion 8 evidence — a category many tech petitioners struggle to document. The gap is converting internal executive achievements into externally-validated, field-wide influence."\n  },\n  "risksAndMitigation": [\n    {\n      "risk": "Executive Role Mistaken for Internal Management",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "USCIS frequently denies tech executive EB-1As when contributions appear confined to employer-internal impact rather than field-wide influence. Vedh's bullets currently describe DevCare/Avtech internal deliverables.",\n      "mitigation": "Reframe every accomplishment with external metrics: client adoption beyond contracted scope, open-source release of accelerators, citations of architectural patterns, third-party press coverage."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Ambiguous Authorship Claim",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "Resume opens with 'accomplished author' but no specific publications are cited. USCIS will scrutinize and potentially issue an RFE if authorship is self-published, blog-only, or non-scholarly.",\n      "mitigation": "Either substantiate existing book/articles with sales, citations, and reviews — or rapidly publish 3-4 peer-reviewed/IEEE-tier articles in Phase 3 to backfill Criterion 6."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Internal Awards Discounted",\n      "severity": "Medium",\n      "description": "Both documented awards (CBA CEO Best Team 2009, Kony Best Mobile Architecture) are internal employer awards, which USCIS adjudicators routinely reject as insufficient for Criterion 1.",\n      "mitigation": "Pursue 2-3 industry-judged awards (Globee, Stevie, CIO 100) in Phase 5 with documented external judging panels and selection criteria."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "No Judging Experience",\n      "severity": "Medium",\n      "description": "Mentoring internal teams does not satisfy Criterion 4. Without external judging credentials, Vedh has only 2 strong criteria, falling short of the 3-criterion minimum.",\n      "mitigation": "Phase 4 prioritizes 2-3 judging engagements (awards panels, journal peer review, hackathon judging) to lock in Criterion 4 within 6 months."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Lack of Independent Expert Letters",\n      "severity": "Medium",\n      "description": "Letters only from former colleagues/managers carry minimal weight. EB-1A petitions need 4-5 independent experts who know Vedh through reputation/publications, not direct work.",\n      "mitigation": "Use Forbes Council network, conference appearances, and published whitepapers to build genuine independent relationships before requesting letters in Phase 5."\n    }\n  ],\n  "confidenceAnalysis": {\n    "currentConfidenceLow": 25,\n    "currentConfidenceHigh": 35,\n    "currentLabel": "HIGH RISK OF DENIAL OR RFE",\n    "postConfidenceLow": 75,\n    "postConfidenceHigh": 85,\n    "postLabel": "STRONG APPROVAL LIKELIHOOD",\n    "timelineMonths": "11-14",\n    "upliftMessage": "Following this roadmap shifts Vedh's petition from a likely RFE/denial scenario to a strong approval profile — a ~50 percentage point uplift driven primarily by external validation, scholarly publishing, and judging credentials.",\n    "currentMetrics": {\n      "strongCriteria": "2 of 10 (Membership, Leading Role)",\n      "independentLetters": "0 confirmed",\n      "judgingCredentials": "None established",\n      "rfeRisk": "Very High (70-80%)"\n    },\n    "postMetrics": {\n      "strongCriteria": "5-6 of 10",\n      "independentLetters": "4-5 confirmed independent + 3-4 dependent",\n      "judgingCredentials": "Globee/Stevie panel + IEEE peer reviewer",\n      "rfeRisk": "Low-Moderate (20-30%)"\n    }\n  }\n}	EB-1A	2026-05-04 17:45:46.972+00	2026-05-04 18:51:05.512+00	elite_blueprint	https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/cs_live_a1uABrJtcGYVuhMdan2LlDqwOHloP0a7l68VSeRlofBIz2Kt5Osopkznop#fidnandhYHdWcXxpYCc%2FJ2FgY2RwaXEnKSdicGRmZGhqaWBTZHdsZGtxJz8nZmprcXdqaScpJ2R1bE5gfCc%2FJ3VuWml