6	Arvind K	akandula0309@gmail.com	16148229867	\N	\N	booth	Event: TACO2026 · Visa interest: Not sure	\N	\N	AI	\N	f	f	f	converted	invited	45	2026-04-24 01:15:04.602871+00	\n\nEeeeks \n \n \nAn accomplished author and digital enablement and transformation visionary with 22+ years of experience, strong focus, and \npassion towards solving business problems and exploring opportunities through ideation, conceptualization, analysis, and \nimplementation of emerging technologies while taking organizations to next-level growth through innovation. Built cases for \ntechnology establishment and adoption while working towards process maturity of the organization. \n \nAPI and Microservices Architecture || Digital Transformation || Cloud Migration and Transformation || Cloud Adoption Strategy \n|| Cloud Migration Patterns || Conversational Apps || AI and ML || RPA Reference Architecture and Strategy || Data Strategy || \nStrategic Roadmap Development || Enterprise Architecture Practices || DevOps Strategy || People Management || IT Cost \nOptimization || Proof-Of-Concept driven decision making || Mobility Solution Architecture  \n \nEnterprise Architecture: Target and Transition State Architectures to empower the team to maintain EA standards \nCloud  Adoption Strategy: Led  a  team  to  design  and  develop  the  future  state  cloud  architecture  for  an  application \nportfolio while building a case for significant cost saving and bringing operational efficiency. \nArtificial Intelligence: Led a team to build Conversational Apps Reference Architecture in 4 weeks’ timeline for a State \nGovernment Agency. \nCMMI: Established CMMI process maturity at DevCare Solutions and enabled the organization to achieve CMMI Maturity \nLevel 3 accreditation. Enabled multiple process dictionaries for project teams’ adoption. \n \nDevCare Solutions | VP - Innovation & Technology (Chief Technology Officer) | August 2021 – Current \n• Leading the entire technology organization consisting of more than 200+ employees. \n• Laying annual strategy for technology enablement and upliftment. \n• Working with the Sales team on Business Development and Sales models and approaches. \n• Providing guidance to the Sales team on identifying potential clients. \n• Guiding the project teams towards successful project delivery by enabling best IT Architecture practices and \nprinciples. \n• Directly leading a team for Innovation and R&D efforts by identifying common business problems and building \naccelerated frameworks for clients IT ecosystem, which significantly reduce the schedule and costs of project \nimplementations. \n• Reviewing and approving project budgets. \n• Developing and providing quarterly technology forecasted expenditure. \n• Establishing and monitoring CMMI process maturity guidelines and ensuring project teams meet the guidelines, \nimproving the overall organizational delivery performance. \n \nAvtech Solutions Inc| Chief Architect | August 2018 – August 2021 \n• Leading day-to-day technology operations and process improvements. \n• Provided architecture solutions and thought leadership for several clients such as Molina Healthcare, Cardinal \nHealth, La-Z-Boy, State of Michigan & State of Ohio  \n• Roadmap for transforming 1700 web services to REST APIs and Microservices.  \n• Managed end-to-end pre-sales efforts for various existing and prospective clients. \n• Led two key product development efforts (Chatbot Accelerator & API Accelerator). \n• Project cost estimation and thereby maintaining burn charts to ensure projects remain on-track from a \nfinancial and budgetary perspective. \n \nState of Ohio – Job & Family Services | Sr. Enterprise Architect (Contractor) | Jan 2019 – June 2019 \nARVIND KANDULA \nCHIEF TECHNOLOGY OFFICER \n“Enabling success and business value through technology focused Thought Leadership.” \n \narvind.kandula@devcare.com   | 614-822-9867 | CMMI Certified | Forbes Technology Council Member \nKey Focus Areas & Strengths \nKey IT & Business Leadership Accomplishments \nCareer History – Key Highlights \n\n• Enabled API Management Platform Strategy by evaluating best fit tools and applicability to JFS. \n• Laid the RPA adoption strategy and provided a decoupled architecture to work across most use cases. \n• Provided end to end architecture for automated employee offboarding. \n• Guiding the EA team with best practices for EA adoption and mentoring on ABACUS (tool for EA). \n \nVoya Financial (Formerly ING) | Enterprise Architect (Contractor) | Aug 2018 - Jan 2019 \n• Responsible for overall cloud (AWS) migration strategy while leading a team of 3 architects. \n• Provided reusable patterns for application group migration to AWS. \n• Provided thought leadership to the team in enabling cost efficient and scalable architecture. \n• Guided the team to adopt MVP pattern to migrate and then transform in the cloud environment. \n• Provided future state AWS architecture by adopting native AWS offerings for operational efficiency. \n• Enabled the team with AWS knowledge by providing insights on best practices for Cloud Architecture. \n \n Nationwide Mutual Insurance | Enterprise Systems Architect | Sep 2014 to Aug 2018 \n• Portfolio Architect for three business units responsible for effective architecture of 18 applications. \n• Led a program of $8+ M in budget to successful architecture adoption. \n• Guided and Mentored a team to build cloud architecture for a suite of 8 applications. \n• Worked with a team of 5 architects towards adoption of Enterprise Architecture principles and \nmethodologies. \n• Provided thought leadership to teams for technology adoption by building appropriate business cases. \n• Mentored developers, tech leads and architects to develop an architectural mindset and apply the principles. \n• Developed deep partnerships with business to influence technology adoption. \n• Led a team to develop proof-of-concepts for native AWS cloud adoption and conversational apps (chatbots). \n \nWells Fargo Advisors | Systems Architect (Contractor) | Sep 2013 to Sep 2014 \n• Portfolio architect leading the customer, account, and document domains. \n• Responsible for providing end-to-end architecture for onboarding and e-fulfillment processes. \n• Provided end-to-end architecture of reusable document storage and e-signature processes. \n• Guided a team of 6 developers for design and implementation of account origination web services. \n \nKony Solutions Inc | Solutions Architect | Feb 2011 to Sep 2013 \n• Responsible for leading architectures of all mobile banking programs within the organization. \n• Provided resilient cross platform mobile architecture for 8 large scale Financial Services organizations. \n• Provided thought leadership and consulting to senior leadership on mobile industry best practice. \n• Guided the team to adopt API first strategy to build reusable components across mobile platforms. \n• Recognized with the Best Mobile Architecture award from the CEO based on client feedback provided. \n \nCommonwealth Bank of Australia | Integration Architect | Oct 2008 to Jan 2011 \n• Worked on the prestigious Core Banking Modernization effort and led a team of 8 service designers. \n• Responsible for leading Account Origination and Account Maintenance SOA teams. \n• Provided architecture for over 40 web services and ensured the team provided optimum designs. \n• Worked with the development team/s to ensure the web services are built according to the design. \n• Led a team of 4 service designers ensuring all design aspects are bug free. \n• Won the CEO Best Team Award (2009)  \n \nQantas Airways | Oracle EBS Team Lead – 2006 to 2008 \nInfinite Computer Solutions | Oracle Financial Analyzer Team Lead | 2003 to 2006     \n    \n \nExecutive Masters in Business Administration | International Business Management Institute | 2021 \nMaster of Information Technology | University of Sydney | 2003 \nBachelor of Computer Applications | Osmania University | 2001 \nGraduate Diploma in Computer Applications | JNNYC | 1998 \n \nEducational Milestones 	Resume-Arvind_Kandula.pdf	{\n  "prospectName": "Arvind K",\n  "visaCategory": "EB-1A",\n  "generatedDate": "May 1, 2026",\n  "executiveSummary": {\n    "strongCriteria": 2,\n    "partialCriteria": 4,\n    "yearsExperience": "22+ years",\n    "approvalRateContext": "EB-1A approval rates for technology executives without academic publications hover around 55-65%. Industry CTOs face heightened scrutiny under the Kazarian two-step analysis, particularly on 'original contributions of major significance' and 'scholarly authorship.'"\n  },\n  "visaOverview": {\n    "whatItIs": "EB-1A is a self-petitioned employment-based green card for individuals at the very top of their field. For Arvind, who is currently a CTO at DevCare Solutions, Forbes Technology Council member, and CMMI-certified architect with 22+ years across Commonwealth Bank, Nationwide, Voya, Wells Fargo, and state government clients, EB-1A is the most viable path because it requires no employer sponsorship or PERM labor certification.",\n    "howToQualify": [\n      "Demonstrate sustained national or international acclaim in enterprise architecture, AI/cloud transformation, or digital enablement",\n      "Satisfy at least 3 of the 10 USCIS criteria with documented, verifiable evidence",\n      "Pass Kazarian Step 2 — a final merits determination showing Arvind is among the small percentage at the top of his field",\n      "Show intent to continue working in the same field (CTO/Enterprise Architecture leadership) in the U.S."\n    ]\n  },\n  "criteriaAssessment": [\n    {\n      "criterion": "Awards/prizes for excellence",\n      "status": "partial",\n      "currentEvidence": "CEO Best Team Award at Commonwealth Bank of Australia (2009) for Core Banking Modernization; Best Mobile Architecture award from Kony Solutions CEO based on client feedback",\n      "gaps": "Both awards are internal/employer-issued, which USCI