24	Naveen Anne	naveenanne8@gmail.com	+1 6146029986	Executive Director - Software Engineering	\N	manual	\N	\N	\N	AI, Information Technology	\N	f	f	f	converted	invited	52	2026-05-19 17:43:59.081061+00	Naveen Anne \n\nExecutive Director | Digital| IT | Middleware Services| Production Support| Infrastructure | Monitoring | SRE – Site Reliability Engineering | Banking Domain\n\nNaveenanne8@gmail.com | (614) 602 9986 \n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/naveen-anne-a23b2613b/ \n\nSummary \n\n➢ Build High-Performing Global Lean Teams: Recruit, Lead, Mentor and Manage diverse, dynamic, high performing, global lean teams of highly motivated, passionate and technical engineers & managers. \n\n➢ Optimize Cost: Introduce end to end Automation, break organization barriers, build lean efficient & accountable teams with broader responsibilities and improve overall operational efficiency \n\n➢ Transformation: Transition support from Application development teams. Partner with Application Development teams, define Non-Functional Requirements NFR’s and Transform high velocity distributed services to Open-source, Cloud, Containers, Modern platform and support them. \n\n➢ Production Support: Lead Priority 1 incidents with best practice troubleshooting, pro-active monitoring, capacity planning, automation, administration for organization critical applications. \n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE \n\nWells Fargo, Charlotte, NC                 Sept’24 - Current \n\nExecutive Director - Software Engineering Senior Manager \n\nSRE Platform support manager for a global team of 30 resources supporting 170 applications in Wells Fargo, CT LOB - Consumer Technology, Home Lending, Servicing Product Area.  These applications are critical applications that service Wells Fargo Mortgage customers on multiple sub products related to Home Lending and hosted across multiple production servers/ Cloud/ Azure platforms running on multiple OS platforms/technologies/ frameworks. \n\nServicing: Manage the mortgage account, statements, apply payments to mortgage account and administer escrow\n\nDefault and Hardship: Manage delinquency offer customer assistance for a loan modification following investor/agency guidelines, manage bankruptcy, foreclosure and litigation.\n\nAccount Management: Manage loans portfolio, title curing, service transfer, lien release, portfolio health, loan recast, escrow account management, property tax, regulatory changes and customer communications.\n\nCustomer Support Services: Agent assisted Telephone customer support channel for mortgage and home equity accounts.\n\nHome Preservation: Provide help to customers to resolve hardship through Loan modification as well as payment assistance mechanisms to keep the customer in their homes.\n\nAsset Management: Management of vendors, invoices and claims and tasks to maintain the property asset while executing foreclosure , auction or liquidation process.\n\nBankruptcy: Process and respond to court ordered bankruptcy case mandates and ensure compliance throughout the bankruptcy process specific for residential home mortgages.\n\nLitigation Management: Manage the mortgage HELOC specific foreclosure and bankruptcy attorney network as well as reviewing quality of work by contracted attorney firms.\n\nWells Fargo, Charlotte, NC |\tApril’22 – Sept’24  | Vice President - Software Engineering Manager \n\nPlatform support manager for a global team of 25 resources that supported 60+ applications in Wells Fargo, WIMT LOB - Wealth & Investment Management Technology, Financial Products Area - supporting 3 product areas Banking, Lending & Investment Solutions. These applications have 3000+ batch jobs and 300+ Web Services hosted across multiple production servers/ Internal Cloud/ Azure / Mainframe platforms running on multiple OS platforms/technologies/ frameworks. \n\nJP Morgan Chase & Co, Columbus, OH |Apr ’13 – Apr’22 | Vice President - Applications Support \n\nBuilt & Led an extremely talented diverse global lean team that transitioned support from Application Development team (40+ Vertical Scrum teams ~ 350 + developers) and supported multiple critical applications in Chase. These applications have 2400+ webservices with 10 Billion+ monthly financial transactions hosted across 350+ production servers/ Internal Cloud/ Kubernetes platforms with a peak average of over 15000 TPS running on multiple OS platforms/technologies/ frameworks and are used by\n\nLine of Business such as Chase.com/Digital, Branches, Teller, IVR, Call centers, ATM’s, Debit/ Credit cards, Mortgage, Auto ..( 200 + internal Clients).\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\nDrive/Lead Transformation Strategy and Execution \n\n✓ Transition support from App Dev team and built an extremely talented horizontal Diverse Platform teams supporting all the needs of 40+ vertical scrum teams responsible for providing front line production support, pro Active monitoring, capacity planning, administration, automation, deployment support and maintenance activities. \n\n✓ This helped Application Development teams to better focus on development work and project deliverables. \n\n✓ Partnered with Application Development teams to define Non-Functional Requirements NFR’s/ Permit To Operate - PTO for the new platform being built to migrate existing platform to Open-source, Cloud, Containers in new datacenter and set support team expectations.\n\n ✓ Built strong working relationship and partnership within immediate sphere of Production \n\nManagement teams, Application teams - CTO, Directors/ Leads, Clients, Global technology teams (network, DBA, AIX) as well as strong partnership with external partners. \n\nProduction Support – The role as a SRE Platform Support Manager is extremely fast paced where in decisions need to be made quickly and effectively to mitigate business impact. Slow or indecision could lead to additional financial/ customer impact to the business. \n\n✓ Lead Priority 1 incidents with best practice troubleshooting to address production issues asap with minimal impact to Business by engaging cross functional teams as needed. ✓ Partnered with various teams as part of Problem Management and did RCA (Root Cause Analysis) to provide long term solutions which ensure a stable production environment. ✓ Kept Management, key stakeholders and business partners well informed on a timely basis on progress, status for Production emergency outages and provided them with root-cause analysis, post mortem and executive reports. \n\n✓ Work closely with clients, vendors, PAC and other technical staff to identify and resolve issues that impact Middleware applications space. \n\n✓  Troubleshoot various middleware, server, load balancer, application, network, database, Datapower, MQ issues in Production hosted across multiple technologies AIX, Linux, Cloud, Docker, Kubernetes, Websphere, Weblogic, Tomcat. \n\n✓ Set up monitoring alerts, dashboards using Splunk, Wily, Prometheus, Grafana and Dynatrace by partnering with the Monitoring Solutions team. \n\n✓ Create and maintain documentation including detailed analysis into the application end to end workflow and infrastructure stack for various critical applications. \n\n✓ Peer reviewed critical change activities and ensured there was no business impact. ✓ Production stability improved and customer impacts reduced significantly ~ 80% since the support was transitioned to dedicated Platform Support team.\n\n\n\nAutomation – Work collaboratively with leadership and cross-organizational delivery teams to discuss requirements and provide automation roadmaps, updates and implement scalable/ maintainable solutions. \n\n✓ Collaborated with App Dev teams and created fully automated Infrastructure with Self Healing, Auto-Scaling, Fail-Over and highly Scalable capabilities which Successfully executed (Zero issues) during peak volume days and holiday seasons (black-Friday, Cyber Monday and Christmas) at record Volumes. \n\n✓ Data center failover workflow for Disaster recovery protocol saved ~ 2hrs of manual effort. ✓ Deployment automation workflow reduced deployment time by ~70%. This also reduced risk and scope for manual errors. \n\n✓ Reduction in MTTR during production outages needing server JVM restarts. ✓ Graceful Auto shutdown of application during scheduled maintenance such as Server Patching and major data center events. \n\n\n\nTeamwork and Leadership – \n\n✓ Hire, mentor and retain employees to build high-performing, self-sufficient diverse global teams. \n\n✓ Influence individuals to take up initiatives and projects via Jira/Kanban that challenge and stretch their technical, business and soft skills. \n\n✓ Motivate the team through regular communications, team building and social events to keep spirits high. \n\n✓ Onboard and cross-train new team members-whilst ensuring committed project milestones are protected. \n\n✓ Manage the performance of the team and conduct quarterly appraisals against set objectives and targets in each individual personal development plan. Identify skill gaps and performance shortfalls and facilitate coaching. \n\n✓ Adhered to the company's IT control policies, architecture standards, risk management, and security policies. \n\n✓ Mentor team members on technology, processes and people leadership \n\nEnvironment: WebSphere, WebLogic, Tomcat, IBM HTTP Server, Apache, IIS; OS Platforms: AIX, Linux, Windows; DataPower, WebSphere Message Broker, Unit test runner, Eclipse/RAD, Tortoise SVN, IBM ClearCase, IBM WebView MQ, F5/Cisco Load balancer, AppViewX, SSL administration, CA Site Minder SSO, WireShark, Network protocols such as TCP/IP,DNS; DHCP; SSH; SFTP; Java/J2EE concepts, ITSM Change Management processes, HP Service manager, service now, Incident management, Problem management, scheduling job tools Control-M, Autosys, and Crontab, DB2, SQL, Oracle, monitoring tools Tivoli, CA Wily Introscope, Splunk, Prometheus, Grafana, Dynatrace; Docker, Kubernetes, Azure, Cloud, Jira, Kanban\n\n\n\nWipro Tech