whatItIs": "EB-1A is a self-petition employment-based first preference green card for individuals at the top of their field. For Kasi — a 20+ year Project Manager / Scrum Master / Product Owner at JPMorgan Chase, GE, Synchrony, and HSBC — this category is challenging because USCIS strongly favors evidence of original contributions of major significance, scholarly authorship, and external recognition rather than internal corporate delivery work.",\n    "howToQualify": [\n      "Satisfy at least 3 of the 10 USCIS regulatory criteria with documented evidence",\n      "Pass the Kazarian two-step review: counting evidence, then 'final merits' totality review",\n      "Demonstrate sustained national or international acclaim — not just internal employer recognition",\n      "Show the U.S. will substantially benefit from your continued work in the field (Agile transformation, digital payments modernization, FinTech)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "criteriaAssessment": [\n    {\n      "criterion": "Awards/prizes for excellence",\n      "status": "weak",\n      "currentEvidence": "Resume references internal performance ratings at Chase but no named awards, industry prizes, or third-party recognized awards",\n      "gaps": "No external awards from PMI, Scrum Alliance, Agile Alliance, Stevie Awards, Globee, Brandon Hall, or industry FinTech bodies",\n      "actionRequired": "Apply to Globee Awards (IT/FinTech), Stevie Awards for Technology Excellence, PMI Project of the Year, and Digital Banker FinTech Awards in 2026 cycle. Also pursue internal Chase 'Above & Beyond' awards documented with letters."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Membership in associations requiring outstanding achievement",\n      "status": "weak",\n      "currentEvidence": "Holds CSP, CSM, CSPO (Scrum Alliance), PMI-ACP, PMI-PMP — these are open certifications, not selective memberships",\n      "gaps": "Certifications do not satisfy this criterion. No senior membership in IEEE, ACM, BCS, or invitation-only bodies",\n      "actionRequired": "Apply for IEEE Senior Member grade (requires 10+ years experience and 3 references — Kasi qualifies), ACM Senior Member, and PMI Fellow nomination track. Join Forbes Technology Council or Fast Company Executive Board (vetted membership)."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Published material about the person",\n      "status": "weak",\n      "currentEvidence": "None documented",\n      "gaps": "No press coverage, podcast interviews, or industry publications featuring Kasi by name",\n      "actionRequired": "Secure feature interviews in CIO.com, InfoQ, Agile Alliance publications, FinTech Magazine, American Banker about digital payments modernization at Chase. Target 3-5 independent third-party features."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Judging others' work",\n      "status": "weak",\n      "currentEvidence": "Internal code reviews and design reviews at Chase, GE, Synchrony — not documented external judging",\n      "gaps": "No peer review for journals, no hackathon judging, no awards panel service",\n      "actionRequired": "Register as reviewer for IEEE Access, IEEE Software, Journal of Systems and Software; judge at AngelHack, Major League Hacking, university capstone competitions; serve on Globee/Stevie Awards judging panels (open applications)."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Original contributions of major significance",\n      "status": "partial",\n      "currentEvidence": "Led monolith-to-microservices decoupling at Chase Digital Payments (UI area block + GKP services), AS400-to-SAP migration at GE SupplierNet, multi-region credit card consolidation at HSBC US/Europe/Canada",\n      "gaps": "Contributions described as employer deliverables, not as field-wide innovations adopted by others; no patents, no widely-cited frameworks, no open-source artifacts",\n      "actionRequired": "Document quantifiable impact (deployment downtime reduction %, $ savings, customers impacted) with letters from senior executives. File 1-2 USPTO provisional patents on payment modernization methodologies. Publish a methodology whitepaper on monolith decoupling adopted beyond Chase."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Authorship of scholarly articles",\n      "status": "weak",\n      "currentEvidence": "None documented",\n      "gaps": "Zero peer-reviewed publications — this is the single biggest gap for a Kazarian final-merits review",\n      "actionRequired": "Author 3-5 articles: (1) IEEE Software conference paper on agile-at-scale in regulated banking; (2) InfoQ article on Cassandra/AWS payment systems; (3) Journal of Financial Technology article; (4) book chapter via IGI Global or Springer on FinTech Agile transformation."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Work displayed at exhibitions",\n      "status": "not_applicable",\n      "currentEvidence": "Not applicable to software/PM field",\n      "gaps": "N/A",\n      "actionRequired": "Skip this criterion — focus elsewhere."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Leading/critical role in distinguished organizations",\n      "status": "partial",\n      "currentEvidence": "Project Manager / Scrum Master / Product Owner roles at JPMorgan Chase (Digital Payments — clearly distinguished), GE Industrial Solutions, Synchrony Financial, and HSBC — all Fortune 500 / globally distinguished",\n      "gaps": "Need documentation that the role was 'leading or critical' — not just a participant. Need org charts, executive letters showing Kasi reported to or advised senior leadership and was indispensable",\n      "actionRequired": "Obtain letters from JPMC Executive Directors / MDs explicitly stating Kasi played a 'critical role' in Chase Digital Payments CXO migration. Same for GE SupplierNet SAP migration lead and Synchrony 9-year tenure. Include org charts and program scope ($ and headcount)."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "High salary",\n      "status": "partial",\n      "currentEvidence": "JPMorgan Chase senior PM/Scrum Master compensation likely in top percentile, but not documented in resume",\n      "gaps": "Need W-2s, offer letters, and BLS/DOL OES wage comparison showing top 10% for SOC code 15-1199 / 11-3021 in NYC or Columbus metro",\n      "actionRequired": "Compile last 3 years W-2s, RSU vesting statements, and pull DOL OES + Levels.fyi data showing Kasi's total comp exceeds 90th percentile for IT Project Managers nationally."\n    },\n    {\n      "criterion": "Commercial success in performing arts",\n      "status": "not_applicable",\n      "currentEvidence": "Not applicable",\n      "gaps": "N/A",\n      "actionRequired": "Skip."\n    }\n  ],\n  "roadmapPhases": [\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 1,\n      "title": "Phase 1 — Evidence Audit & Documentation Foundation",\n      "timeline": "Months 1-2",\n      "urgency": "Start immediately",\n      "steps": [\n        "Compile complete tenure documentation across JPMC (2016-present), GE (2014-2016), Synchrony (2005-2014), HSBC (2004-2005) including org charts, role scope, and program $ values",\n        "Pull last 3 years of Chase W-2s, RSUs, bonus statements and benchmark against DOL OES 90th percentile for SOC 15-1199 / 11-3021",\n        "Quantify impact metrics for the Chase CXO migration, GE SupplierNet SAP cutover, HSBC US/EU/Canada consolidation — deployment downtime %, customers served, $ saved",\n        "Identify 8-10 potential recommenders: 4-5 from current/former employers (Chase MDs, GE leadership, Synchrony, HSBC) and 4-5 truly independent industry experts who have never managed Kasi"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 2,\n      "title": "Phase 2 — Build Original Contributions Evidence",\n      "timeline": "Months 2-5",\n      "urgency": "Begin in parallel",\n      "steps": [\n        "File 1-2 USPTO provisional patents on novel methodologies — e.g., 'Method for decoupling monolithic payment UI from services using GKP/Cassandra' based on Chase Digital Payments work",\n        "Publish a detailed methodology whitepaper (LinkedIn long-form + Medium + InfoQ) on agile-at-scale in regulated FinTech, with case study data",\n        "Open-source a reference framework or toolkit (e.g., a Scrum maturity assessment template, a payments rewrite playbook) on GitHub and track adoption metrics",\n        "Speak at 2-3 conferences: Agile Alliance Agile20XX, Scrum Gathering, FinTech Connect, or PMI Global Summit — submit proposals immediately for 2026 cycle"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 3,\n      "title": "Phase 3 — Scholarly Authorship Push",\n      "timeline": "Months 3-7",\n      "urgency": "Concurrent with Phase 2",\n      "steps": [\n        "Author and submit 1 IEEE Software or IEEE Access article on 'Agile Scaling in Regulated Banking: Lessons from Digital Payments Modernization'",\n        "Submit 1 article to Journal of Systems and Software or International Journal of Project Management on rewrite/migration governance",\n        "Co-author a Springer or IGI Global book chapter on FinTech transformation (these accept industry practitioners with strong experience)",\n        "Publish 2-3 InfoQ / DZone / TechBeacon technical articles to build citation footprint and Google Scholar presence"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 4,\n      "title": "Phase 4 — Judging, Memberships & Peer Review",\n      "timeline": "Months 4-8",\n      "urgency": "Concurrent with Phase 3",\n      "steps": [\n        "Apply for IEEE Senior Member grade (10+ years experience + 3 references — Kasi qualifies easily) and ACM Senior Member",\n        "Register as a peer reviewer for IEEE Access, IEEE Software, and Journal of Financial Technology — complete 3-5 reviews and document them",\n        "Apply to judge Globee Awards, Stevie American Business Awards (Technology category), and Brandon Hall HCM Excellence Awards — all accept open applications",\n        "Judge at 2-3 hackathons (Major League Hacking, AngelHack, university FinTech capstones) and document with certificates"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 5,\n      "title": "Phase 5 — Awards, Press & Expert Recommendation Letters",\n      "timeline": "Months 6-11",\n      "urgency": "Critical for Filing",\n      "steps": [\n        "Submit nominations for Globee IT World Awards, Stevie Awards Technology Executive of the Year, PMI Distinguished Contribution Award, and Digital Banker FinTech awards",\n        "Secure 3-4 independent third-party media features (CIO.com, American Banker, FinTech Magazine, InfoQ podcast) — engage a tech PR consultant if needed",\n        "Draft and finalize 6-8 recommendation letters: 4 independent (from non-employer industry experts at Goldman, Wells Fargo, Capital One, or academia) and 2-4 from current/former senior leaders, each citing specific Kazarian criteria",\n        "Apply to Forbes Technology Council membership (vetted, satisfies association criterion strengthening)"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      "phaseNumber": 6,\n      "title": "Phase 6 — Petition Assembly, Legal Review & Filing",\n      "timeline": "Months 11-14",\n      "urgency": "Critical for Filing",\n      "steps": [\n        "Engage an EB-1A specialist immigration attorney (not a generalist) — interview 3, prefer one with FinTech/IT executive track record",\n        "Assemble exhibit binder organized by Kazarian criterion — target 4-5 strong criteria (Original Contributions, Scholarly Authorship, Judging, Critical Role, High Salary)",\n        "Draft a compelling 25-35 page petition letter weaving narrative around Chase Digital Payments leadership and FinTech impact, with national-interest framing",\n        "File I-140 with Premium Processing ($2,805 PP fee) for 15-day adjudication; prepare RFE response templates in advance for likely 'original contributions' challenge"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  "profileRarity": {\n    "stats": [\n      {"value": "20+", "label": "Years in Software/PM", "sublabel": "Spanning developer to PM/PO/Scrum Master"},\n      {"value": "4", "label": "Fortune 500 / Global Banks", "sublabel": "JPMC, GE, Synchrony, HSBC"},\n      {"value": "5+", "label": "Agile Certifications", "sublabel": "CSP, CSM, CSPO, PMI-ACP, PMP"},\n      {"value": "9", "label": "Years at Synchrony", "sublabel": "Demonstrated sustained tenure & impact"}\n    ],\n    "competitiveAdvantage": "Kasi's two-decade trajectory across four globally distinguished financial institutions — anchored by current leadership in JPMorgan Chase Digital Payments modernization — provides a strong 'Critical Role' and 'High Salary' foundation rare among IT PM petitioners. However, USCIS adjudicators routinely deny corporate-IT EB-1A petitions that lack scholarly authorship, patents, or external recognition; Kasi's profile must be aggressively augmented in those areas to convert tenure into 'sustained acclaim'."\n  },\n  "risksAndMitigation": [\n    {\n      "risk": "Corporate IT/PM Profile Without Scholarly Output",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "EB-1A adjudicators are skeptical of project manager profiles, viewing the work as employer-specific delivery rather than field-wide contribution. Without papers, patents, or citations, the Kazarian 'final merits' review typically fails.",\n      "mitigation": "Execute Phase 2 and 3 aggressively — produce at least 3 peer-reviewed or industry publications, 1-2 patents, and an open-source artifact within 6 months."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Internal Recognition Mistaken for Acclaim",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "Resume relies on Chase performance ratings and employer-recognized impact. USCIS explicitly discounts internal awards as evidence of national/international acclaim.",\n      "mitigation": "Pursue 2-3 external industry awards (Globee, Stevie, PMI) and secure independent media coverage from outlets unaffiliated with Chase."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Certifications Misclassified as Selective Memberships",\n      "severity": "Medium",\n      "description": "PMI-PMP, CSM, CSPO are open-enrollment credentials and do not satisfy Criterion 2. Petition will be weakened if these are submitted under that criterion.",\n      "mitigation": "Achieve IEEE Senior Member and ACM Senior Member status (both require peer evaluation) and join Forbes Technology Council before filing."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "Lack of Independent Recommenders",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "Letters only from Chase/GE/Synchrony colleagues will be discounted as biased. USCIS expects 50%+ of letters from independent experts who never worked with the petitioner.",\n      "mitigation": "Build relationships now with senior FinTech leaders at peer institutions (Goldman, Capital One, Wells Fargo) and academic researchers in software engineering — through conference speaking and peer review."\n    },\n    {\n      "risk": "RFE on Original Contributions of Major Significance",\n      "severity": "High",\n      "description": "This is the most-challenged criterion for IT petitioners. Adjudicators want evidence the work influenced the field beyond the employer.",\n      "mitigation": "File patents, publish methodology adopted by others (track GitHub stars, citations, downloads), and obtain expert letters explicitly stating the Chase/GE work influenced industry practice."\n    }\n  ],\n  "confidenceAnalysis": {\n    "currentConfidenceLow": 15,\n    "currentConfidenceHigh": 25,\n    "currentLabel": "HIGH RISK OF DENIAL OR RFE",\n    "postConfidenceLow": 65,\n    "postConfidenceHigh": 80,\n    "postLabel": "STRONG APPROVAL LIKELIHOOD",\n    "timelineMonths": "11-14",\n    "upliftMessage": "Following this roadmap raises Kasi's EB-1A approval likelihood from ~15-25% (high RFE/denial risk) to ~65-80% (strong approval) by converting corporate tenure into documented external acclaim.",\n    "currentMetrics": {\n      "strongCriteria": "1 of 10 (Critical Role partially)",\n      "independentLetters": "0 confirmed",\n      "judgingCredentials": "None established",\n      "rfeRisk": "Very High (75-85%)"\n    },\n    "postMetrics": {\n      "strongCriteria": "4-5 of 10",\n      "independentLetters": "4-6 confirmed",\n      "judgingCredentials": "IEEE Senior Member + journal reviewer + awards judge",\n      "rfeRisk": "Low-Moderate (20-30%)"\n    }\n  }\n}	EB-1A	2026-04-30 19:08:09.171+00	2026-05-15 14:50:54.44+00	elite_blueprint	https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/cs_live_a1m4shyjlEKJ2HPh9cW4qxyRTuhupn2cli8phYp6KpwKmn2nGKgb7rcLsj#fidnandhYHdWcXxpYCc%2FJ2FgY2RwaXEnKSdicGRmZGhqaWBTZHdsZGtxJz8nZmprcXdqaScpJ2R1bE5gfCc%2FJ3VuWmlsc2BaMDRRRmhwSERAclVQRjFPSWh3NGZIQDNuTFU8UlNDMkpgX3ZgSzZLdzVQR21qf3NJdDdMNTxOUnBGUlJoc3VTSHBcTzBwQkpAbVE3SWNjbTNPMmliVmJqXWI1NT1iX2BCbzRXJyknY3dqaFZgd3Ngdyc%2FcXdwYCknZ2RmbmJ3anBrYUZqaWp3Jz8nJmNjY2NjYycpJ2lkfGpwcVF8dWAnPyd2bGtiaWBabHFgaCcpJ2BrZGdpYFVpZGZgbWppYWB3dic%2FcXdwYHgl	\N	cs_live_a1m4shyjlEKJ2HPh9cW4qxyRTuhupn2cli8phYp6KpwKmn2nGKgb7rcLsj	2026-05-15 14:50:39.514+00	Pinnacle_Cube_EB1A_Roadmap_Kasi.pdf		t	\N
