id control modules \n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to identify, analyze, and resolve powertrain issues through root cause \nanalysis and corrective action development \n• Contribute  to Cybersecurity feature  development,  including  Authenticated  Diagnostic  Access  (ADA)  for \nelectric powertrain modules \n• Execute unit testing using tools such as T32 Lauterbach, ETAS INCA and Vector CANoe to diagnose and fix in-\nvehicle issues \n• Streamline daily engineering processes by automating repetitive tasks with Python thereby reducing manual \neffort by 80% \n• Strategically forecast and plan ECU resource (CPU, RAM and ROM) allocation for multiple electric and hybrid \nvehicle projects to optimize performance and efficiency \n \nHardware Engineer - Intel Corporation                                             June,2017 – October,2019  \n• Conducting Safety, EMC and RF pre-certification tests & diagnosis for Intel products at internal laboratories  \n• Managing internal & external product regulatory global conformity assessment activities   \n• As Chairperson for Energy Efficiency Center of Excellence, establishing proactive strategies to ensure robust \ninternal energy compliance programs for all business units  \n• Reviewing test data provided by 3\nrd\n party test labs and approving for full regulatory certification  \n\n• Comprehending implications of new technologies from regulatory standpoint  \n• Guiding product development teams to make better products by reviewing specifications & design concepts  \n• Provided  regulatory  direction  for  NUC,  a mini-PC developed  by  Intel  which  enabled  product  sales  in  69 \ncountries thereby giving the organization $90M in revenue  \n \nGraduate Technical Intern - Intel Corporation                             May- December,2016  \n• Developed a new testing procedure named “Reasonable Basis EMI Probe Technique” in collaboration with my \nmentor, which improved the testing throughput time by 83% and employee productivity by 61% in the pilot \nrun     \n• Invented a novel noise filtration algorithm using predictive analytical techniques and MATLAB to filter various \nambient noises from measured radiated emissions data \n• Achieved  85%  noise  cancelation  with  the  new  algorithm  while  traditional  algorithms just gave  50% \ncancelation  \n• Proposed  an  innovative  emergency  evacuation  plan  which  is  based  on  Internet  of Things  (IoT)  &  built  a \nprototype using 3D printer \n• Built an automated tool using VBA, which improved the pre-compliance assessment time by 80%  \n• Performed radiated emissions testing on various Intel products to meet FCC regulatory specifications \n \nElectrical Engineering - Teaching Labs, UTD                                      July,2015 – May,2016; February – May,2017  \n• Troubleshooted Multimeters, Oscilloscopes, Signal Generators and Power Supplies with measurement issues  \n• Tested equipment to ensure proper functionality  \n \nRF & Microwave Measurements Laboratory, UTD                               January - May,2016  \n• Designed various circuits in the Lab like Microstrip resonators, Wilkinson power divider, Branch- line coupler, \n20dB Edge- coupler, Chebyshev & Butterworth filters, Broadband Amplifier etc. Tested these milled circuits  \n \nCenter for Computer Science Education & Outreach, UTD                                                 October,2015 - May,2016   \n• Introduced tools like Scratch, Alice and Logo to school students and helped them develop problem solving skills  \n \nInternship at Bharat Sanchar Nijam Limited (BSNL), India                                                                   May- June,2012  \n• Acquired knowledge on wireless communication technologies & hardware implementation of the networks \n \nAcademic Projects  \nPhysical Chip Design of LNA RFIC at 1.84GHz   \n• Analyzed and designed a single stage cascoded LNA using IBM 130nm Technology  \n• Attained  a  noise  figure  of  1.23  dB,  linear  gain  of  18.54  dB,  IIP3  of -4.60  dBm,  S11  of -31.11dB  and  S22  of -\n24.91dB with the operating range between 1.8052-1.8798 GHz along with 10% variation tolerance   \nDrone based delivery system   \n• Designed the radar circuit that is to be installed on the drone, used for detecting the destination point  \n• Simulated the communication links between the radar, drone and the base station using AWR-VSS software \nAdaptive Water Sprinkler Using Raspberry Pi (IoT)  \n• Prepared  a  smart  water  sprinkler and  programmed  it  using  Python  language, which  operates  considering \nparameters like soil moisture, humidity and   temperature of surroundings.  \n• The sensor data is processed using Raspberry Pi and thereby the sprinkler is controlled.  \n\nRF Based Remote Controlled Robot  \n•      Designed a circuit to control the robot remotely by making use of the RF modules  \n \nEducation  \nMaster of Science in Electrical Engineering                                                       May,2017  \nThe University of Texas at Dallas (UTD) - USA                                                  \nBachelor of Technology in Electronics and Communications Engineering  June,2014  \nK L University - India       \n                                                                                \nPatents and Publications  \n• Patent US10338120B2: For  the  innovation  in  radiated  emissions  testing  techniques  titled “Methods and \nApparatus to Analyze Radio Frequency Emissions from Devices”   \n• Research  paper  on "Implementation  of  Ionospheric  Prediction  Algorithm  Based  on  Huang  Hilbert \ntransform" published in IEEE digital Xplore (http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/ICSPCT.2014.6884988)  \n \nAchievements                      \n• Successfully led the Energy Star initiative, which helped a NUC (mini-PC) product to become a pioneer in  \nIntel’s history to be Energy Star certified   \n• Runner up - Intel maker's challenge contest for the prototype on Intelligent Emergency Evacuation System  \n• Recognized as best intern during Internship at BSNL, India   \n 	Neelima_Velagapudi_Resume_042026.pdf	\N	\N	\N	2026-05-04 20:19:24.769+00	elite_blueprint	https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/cs_live_a1UQZYLDR76hX570y5P879e2u0TLrN32moQgPJu7G2ijo3oqbM7KhA2Vhu#fidnandhYHdWcXxpYCc%2FJ2FgY2RwaXEnKSdicGRmZGhqaWBTZHdsZGtxJz8nZmprcXdqaScpJ2R1bE5gfCc%2FJ3VuWmlsc2BaMDRRRmhwSERAclVQRjFPSWh3NGZIQDNuTFU8UlNDMkpgX3ZgSzZLdzVQR21qf3NJdDdMNTxOUnBGUlJoc3VTSHBcTzBwQkpAbVE3SWNjbTNPMmliVmJqXWI1NT1iX2BCbzRXJyknY3dqaFZgd3Ngdyc%2FcXdwYCknZ2RmbmJ3anBrYUZqaWp3Jz8nJmNjY2NjYycpJ2lkfGpwcVF8dWAnPyd2bGtiaWBabHFgaCcpJ2BrZGdpYFVpZGZgbWppYWB3dic%2FcXdwYHgl	\N	cs_live_a1UQZYLDR76hX570y5P879e2u0TLrN32moQgPJu7G2ijo3oqbM7KhA2Vhu	2026-05-04 20:19:15.362+00	Neelima_EB1A_Analysis_Roadmap.pdf		t	\N
