s, and timelines for AI chatbot initiatives.\n\nConducted requirements workshops and interviews with stakeholders to elicit and document business requirements. \n\nImplemented natural language processing techniques to improve chatbot understanding and response accuracy that includes conversational flow design and enhancing the overall user experience for Hagerty’s Claims Application and developing intents using Azure Language Studio.\n\nConducted thorough business process analysis, identifying opportunities for optimization and efficiency improvements.\n\nUtilized data analysis techniques to derive insights from large datasets, providing valuable information for decision-making. \n\nContributed to the development and execution of user acceptance testing (UAT) plans.\n\nCreate status reporting mechanisms to monitor the status of the above activities. Host integration discussions, with representatives of all test teams, identify and help resolve roadblocks. Providing regular reports on chatbot performance, user feedback, and other key metrics, and maintaining comprehensive documentation.\n\nPrepare test protocols and reports which meet regulatory requirements, during the final test cycle. Be the primary advocate for the adoption of methodologies which are appropriate for the project. \n\nActed as a liaison between business stakeholders and technical teams, facilitating communication and ensuring project success.\n\nExtensive knowledge in Developing Reports for business end users using SSRS Report Manager and Tableau.\n\n\n\nJune 2009 to February 2021, Senior Systems Analyst at IBM\n\nProject Name: Anthem INC, Albany, NY\n\nProject Description: \n\nIBM has partnered with Anthem Inc to provide Application Management Services (AMS) and Capabilities in building innovative solutions as well modernizing their legacy systems to increase scale and time to market new products benefiting end healthcare customers in the US to select healthcare of their choice. \n\nIBM’s agreed t