e \nimpediment to ensure that the team is fully functional and productive. \n● Shield the team from external interferences/distractions. \n● Assist with internal and external communication, improving transparency and radiating information. \n● Build a trusting and safe environment where problems can be raised with an emphasis on problem solving. \n● Helped the team to understand the Agile Values and Principles and the benefit of implementing the same. \n● Assess  the  Scrum  Maturity  of  the  team  and  coaching  the  team  to  higher  levels  of  maturity,  at  a  pace  that  is \n sustainable and predictable for the team. \n \nProject # 2 \nClient \nGE – Industrial Solutions \nEnvironment JIRA,  Java,  J2EE,  JSP, EJB,  XML,  Oracle9i  ,  Web  logic  Server  , CICS,  Mainframes, \nTest Director, SVN, MS Visio, Soap UI \nDuration August 2014 to Jan 2016 \n \nProject Description \n \nSupplierNet – It is a workflow-based system used by worldwide GE users and its suppliers. Earlier it was on AS400 and \nbusiness decided to migrate and integrate all its Supply chain to SAP along with new electronic Invoicing and Bill-back \nsystems.  In  this  project  we  need  to  identify  the  impacted  functionality  due  to  migration  where  major  changes  are \ninvolved including external systems that are impacted.   \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n● Rewrite  existing  applications  with the latest  technology  stack  by  co-ordinating  with  multiple  cross  impacts \nteams in  collaboration  with  technical  architects,  business  stakeholders,  senior  management,  product  owners \nand  technical  leads to  define  program  scope,  objectives,  and  deliverables,  ensuring  alignment  with  overall \nbusiness goals. \n● Prepare  program  roadmap,  engage  in  requirement  scoping,  coordinate  effort  estimation,  create  release  plan, \n\nparticipate  in  design  and  architecture  reviews,  facilitate  agile  ceremonies,  track  progress,  monitor  risks, \nprepare mitigation plan, ensure signoffs on deliverables, track metrics data and guide team members to deliver \nthe program as per critical success factors of time, cost, and quality. \n● Remove  technical  impediments  or  guide  the  team  to  remove  impediments  by  finding  the  right  personnel  to \nremove the impediment to ensure that the teams are fully functional and productive. \n● Responsible for creating and managing the release plans. \n● Facilitated   various   Scrum   activities,   such   as   Sprint   Planning,   Daily   Scrum   meeting,   Sprint   Reviews   & \nRetrospectives, Release Planning and Product Backlog refinement to plan future sprints without any delay. \n● Worked  with  product  owners  to  develop  release  plans,  organize  backlog  items  into  priority  groups,  adjusted \nrelease plans following each sprint review. \n● Played all roles in software development i.e., as a developer, tester, business analyst, product owner, project \nmanager, scrum master and scrum professional. \n● Responsible  for  maintaining  clear  and  concise  product  backlog  items  and  organizing  product  backlog  for \nmaximum value and effectiveness.  \n● Creating  projects,  Sprint  Boards  based  on  Remaining  Time/Days  &  USP/Days  for  individual  and  combined \nboard for multiple projects, tracking time, status of each Task etc...in JIRA. \n● Assist with internal and external communication, improving transparency and radiating information. \n● Build a trusting and safe environment where problems can be raised with an emphasis on problem solving. \n● Helped the team to understand the Agile Values and Principles and the benefit of implementing the same. \n \n \n \n \n \nProject # 3 \nClient Synchrony \nEnvironment JIRA,  Rally,  Java,  JSP,  EJB,  XML,  Oracle9i,  Web  logic  Server,  CICS,  Mainframes, \nTest Director, SVN, MS Visio, Soap UI \nDuration Sep 2005 to July 2014 \n \n \nSynchrony is a premier consumer financial services company delivering one of the industry's most  complete digitally-\nenabled product suites. Synchrony experience, expertise and scale encompass a broad spectrum of industries including \ndigital,  health  and  wellness,  retail,  telecommunications,  home,  auto,  outdoors,  pet  and  more.  Synchrony  connects \ntheir  partners  and  consumers  through  our  dynamic  financial  ecosystem  and  provide  them  with  a  diverse  set  of \nfinancing solutions and innovative digital capabilities to address their specific needs and deliver seamless, omnichannel \nexperiences.. \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n● Elicit requirements using interviews, document analysis, requirements workshops, surveys, site visits, business \nprocess descriptions, use cases, scenarios, business analysis, tasks, and workflow analysis. \n● First  analysis  of  the  Work  Requests  and  Change  controls,  its  impact  on  the  existing  system,  identification  of \nrisks,  assumptions  and  impact  on  the third-party systems  that  interact  with  the  application,  involvement  of \nappropriate resources for analysis, documentation, and estimation.  \n● Tracking the Work requests for a release from end-to-end perspective \n● Review  of  the  entire  work  request  after  each  phase  in  person and including  both  functional  and  technical \nteams. \n● Updating of Business Requirement (BR) documents. \n● Scheduling sign-off calls with business to review the requirements and live updating \n● the BR documents if required. \n● Updating process flow diagrams in Visio for the pictorial representation. \n● Updating Functional Design (FD) documents. \n\n● Updating  the  Usability  documents  and  scheduling  call  with  Business/End  User  for  review  and  feedback. \nIncorporating any new requirements based on the feasibility through Change Control Process. \n● Review of the estimations based on the signed-off requirements and if any deviation getting the approval from \nthe business and review of the project plan or timelines. \n● Review  of  the  test  conditions  provided  by  the  business  to  ensure  each  and  every  requirement  and  their \nimpacted functionalities are validated in the testing phase. \n● Analysis of the issues by validating the data loaded in Oracle DB, executing the RPC’s of the host system and \nMiddle-ware logs. \n● Single  point  of  contact  for  the  issues  faced  by  any  team i.e., Build,  QA,  Data  Load,  production  support  and \nBusiness teams. \n● Issue  resolution  (IR)  and  the  first  analysis  of  any  issues  in  the  release  &  Assignment  of  issues  to  different \nteams/ developers involved. \n• Proven  ability  to  influence  the  performance  of  other  associates  and  to  contribute  significant  internal  and \nexternal impacts related to complex business opportunities. \n• Responsible for creating and managing the release plans. \n• Track and communicate Sprint and Release progress of agile projects. \n• Facilitated   various   Scrum   activities   such   as   Sprint   Planning,   Daily   Scrum   meeting,   Sprint   Reviews   & \nRetrospectives, Release Planning and Product Backlog refinement to plan future sprints without any delay. \n• Worked  with  program  management  and  product  owners  to  ensure  product  backlogs  are  well  groomed, \nprioritized  and  visible  to  all  stakeholders.  Worked  with  product  owners  to  develop  release  plans,  organize \nbacklog items into priority groups, adjusted release plans following each sprint review. \n• Product backlog grooming, drafting requirements for user stories, maintaining product/Sprint backlog etc... \n• Responsible for maintaining clear and concise product backlog items. \n• Organizing product backlog for maximum value and effectiveness.  \n• Collaborate  with  team  to  have  real  time  data  in  Burn-Down  charts,  Issue  Tracker,  velocity  chart  and  detailed \nSprint status. \n• Plans/scripts  ensure  that  releases  include  reference  artifacts  for  operational  support,  ensure  that  defect \nmanagement process is incorporated into agile framework. \n• Assist with internal and external communication, improving transparency and radiating information. \n• Build a trusting and safe environment where problems can be raised with an emphasis on problem solving. \n• Coached the team to build incremental working products by working collaboratively with PO and testing team. \n \nAs a Developer,  \n \n● Design \n● Coding  \n● Unit Testing \n● Preparing Unit test cases and test scripts \n \n \nProject # 4 \nClient HSBC US, HSBC EUROPE, HSBC CANADA \nEnvironment COBOL, JCL, CICS, CA-7, Change Man, CA-7, Abend-Aid and File-Aid \nDuration From January 2004 to August 2005 \n \nProject Description \n \nThe  HSBC  Credit  card  processing  can  be  classified  into  two  different  systems i.e., HSBC  US  and  HSBC  Europe.  This \nproject  is  designed  to  allow  Client  to  select  either  US  or  EU  functionality  based  on  the  flags  set  at  the  system  Level.  \nAfter  analyzing  the  entire  processing  of  the  sub  systems,  each  sub  system  is  divided  into  different  functionality i.e., \nEnrollment  processing,  Points  processing, etc... and  programs  were  written  to  include  both  US  and  EU  functionality. \nThere was also little functionality customized for CANADA as this was first Business Unit to use the code. \n\n \nResponsibilities:  \n \n● Design \n● Coding  \n● Unit Testing \n● Preparing Unit test cases and test scripts 	Kasi Kamisetty Software Engineer.pdf	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-06-03 02:32:34.214+00	Pinnacle_Cube_EB1A_Roadmap_Kasi.pdf		t	\N
