EB1A-09	eb1a	09	Commercial success	Evidence of commercial successes in the performing arts, as shown by box office receipts or record, cassette, compact disk, or video sales.	EB1A-09_Commercial_Success	10	f	Upload box office records, streaming numbers, album sales figures, ticket sales, or any official documentation of commercial performance. Include industry benchmark data showing how your results compare to peers in the performing arts.
NIW-04	niw	04	Education and credentials	Advanced degree or exceptional ability demonstrated through academic credentials and professional qualifications.	NIW-04_Education_Credentials	4	t	\N
EB1A-02	eb1a	02	Membership	Documentation of the alien's membership in associations in the field which require outstanding achievements of their members, as judged by recognized national or international experts.	EB1A-02_Membership	2	t	Upload your membership certificate or confirmation letter, the organization's membership criteria page, and any documentation showing the selection process. Evidence that membership requires a vote by existing members or peer review is especially valuable.
EB1A-04	eb1a	04	Judging others	Evidence of the alien's participation, either individually or on a panel, as a judge of the work of others in the same or an allied field.	EB1A-04_Judging_Others	4	t	Upload the formal invitation letter naming you as a judge or reviewer, the event program or panel description, any certificates of participation, and documentation showing the scope of what you reviewed (number of submissions, prestige of the event or journal).
EB1A-06	eb1a	06	Scholarly articles	Evidence of the alien's authorship of scholarly articles in the field, in professional or major trade publications or other major media.	EB1A-06_Scholarly_Articles	6	t	Upload the full text of each published article, the acceptance or publication confirmation email, the journal or conference homepage showing it is a recognized venue, and citation records if available. Include articles where you are a named author — co-authorship counts.
EB1A-10	eb1a	10	Artistic exhibitions	Evidence of the display of the alien's work in the field at artistic exhibitions or showcases.	EB1A-10_Exhibitions	7	f	Upload exhibition catalogs, invitations, photographs of your work on display, press coverage of the exhibition, and documentation of the venue's reputation. Evidence of juried or curated exhibitions is stronger than open-call shows.
NIW-07	niw	07	Support letters	Letters from experts and organizations with firsthand knowledge confirming the national interest and the petitioner's standing.	NIW-07_Support_Letters	7	t	\N
NIW-08	niw	08	Balance of factors	On balance, waiving the job offer and labor certification requirement serves the national interest of the United States.	NIW-08_Balance_of_Factors	8	t	\N
O1A-01	o1	01	Awards and prizes	Documentation of the beneficiary's receipt of nationally or internationally recognized prizes or awards for excellence in the field.	O1A-01_Awards_and_Prizes	1	t	Upload award certificates, nomination letters, and documentation of the award's selectivity and national or international recognition. Include evidence of how recipients are chosen.
O1A-02	o1	02	Membership	Documentation of the beneficiary's membership in associations that require outstanding achievements as judged by recognized experts.	O1A-02_Membership	2	t	Upload membership confirmation, the organization's selection criteria, and evidence that membership requires outstanding achievement as judged by recognized experts in the field.
O1A-03	o1	03	Press coverage	Published material in professional or major trade publications about the beneficiary and the beneficiary's work.	O1A-03_Press_Coverage	3	t	Upload full copies of articles or interviews about you and your work, with documentation of the publication's reach and audience. Coverage in major trade publications or mainstream media carries the most weight.
O1A-04	o1	04	Judging	Evidence of the beneficiary's participation as a judge of the work of others in the same or allied field.	O1A-04_Judging	4	t	Upload your formal invitation to judge, the event or journal description, any participation certificate, and evidence of the scope and prestige of what you reviewed.
NIW-02	niw	02	Well positioned to advance	The petitioner is well positioned to advance the proposed endeavor based on education, skills, knowledge, and record of success in the field.	NIW-02_National_Importance	2	t	Upload your full CV, degrees and transcripts, publications, awards, letters from collaborators confirming your expertise, and any evidence of past success in advancing your proposed endeavor.
NIW-03	niw	03	Balance of factors	On balance, waiving the job offer and labor certification requirement serves the national interest of the United States, as the petitioner's contributions outweigh the national interest in the labor certification process.	NIW-03_Well_Positioned	3	t	Upload evidence that your work uniquely benefits the United States — such as partnerships with US institutions, funding from US government agencies, or documentation that your specific expertise is scarce among US workers. Letters from US employers or institutions are particularly helpful.
O1A-06	o1	06	Scholarly articles	Evidence of the beneficiary's authorship of scholarly articles in professional journals or other major media.	O1A-06_Scholarly_Articles	6	t	Upload full article texts, publication confirmations, journal or conference credentials, and citation records. Co-authored articles where you are a named author are included.
O1A-07	o1	07	Critical or essential role	Evidence of the beneficiary's performance in a critical or essential role for distinguished organizations.	O1A-07_Critical_Role	7	t	Upload your title documentation, org chart, letters describing your specific responsibilities, and evidence of the organization's distinguished reputation — such as revenue figures, industry rankings, or press coverage.
O1A-08	o1	08	High remuneration	Evidence of the beneficiary's high salary or other remuneration for services compared to others in the field.	O1A-08_High_Remuneration	8	t	Upload pay stubs, offer letter, W-2 or equivalent, bonus and equity documentation, and any employer compensation statements. We compare your earnings to industry benchmarks for your role.
